1
00:00:00,480 --> 00:00:01,661
Just imagine for a moment.

2
00:00:02,081 --> 00:00:02,881
Ravi.

3
00:00:02,482 --> 00:00:03,282
A boy from Srikakulam.

4
00:00:03,282 --> 00:00:05,083
Age 27.

5
00:00:05,083 --> 00:00:07,745
A software engineer at an IT company in
Gachibowli.

6
00:00:07,885 --> 00:00:22,035
Every Sankranti, every Dasara, he travels home
from Hyderabad — about 14 hours by bus.

7
00:00:22,055 --> 00:00:24,296
His mother asks: "Ravi, can't you find a job
somewhere here?" Ravi laughs.

8
00:00:24,696 --> 00:00:25,496
"What is there here, Amma?

9
00:00:25,697 --> 00:00:31,982
Everyone is going to Hyderabad, Bangalore,
America." But this Sankranti, he hears

10
00:00:31,982 --> 00:00:33,922
different talk near home.

11
00:00:34,463 --> 00:00:35,343
Google is coming, they say.

12
00:00:35,343 --> 00:00:36,484
A steel plant is coming, they say.

13
00:00:36,484 --> 00:00:38,245
A new airport has opened, they say.

14
00:00:38,525 --> 00:00:42,248
Vizag will become the next Hyderabad, they
say.

15
00:00:42,268 --> 00:00:47,131
At the same time, people are protesting with
placards on Vizag's Beach Road.

16
00:00:47,491 --> 00:00:48,752
"They are cutting our hills.

17
00:00:48,752 --> 00:00:54,936
Our water is going to disappear." So Ravi has
a doubt.

18
00:00:54,996 --> 00:00:55,957
Is this my future?

19
00:00:56,177 --> 00:00:59,879
Or a sacrifice my town is making for someone
else's future?

20
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:04,262
Why is the Chandrababu Naidu government
placing such a big bet on Vizag?

21
00:01:04,643 --> 00:01:06,344
Why lakhs of crores in investment, here?

22
00:01:06,564 --> 00:01:09,606
How much will the people of Andhra really
gain?

23
00:01:09,866 --> 00:01:10,967
How much will they lose?

24
00:01:11,007 --> 00:01:12,668
Let's see the complete story in this video.

25
00:01:13,008 --> 00:01:13,808
With facts.

26
00:01:13,849 --> 00:01:15,190
With arguments from both sides.

27
00:01:15,230 --> 00:01:16,370
The verdict is yours.

28
00:01:16,410 --> 00:01:17,210
Let's begin.

29
00:01:17,371 --> 00:01:23,015
Chapter 1: The Hyderabad Wound.

30
00:01:23,095 --> 00:01:27,758
To understand the story, we have to go back to
2014.

31
00:01:28,158 --> 00:01:30,359
June 2, 2014.

32
00:01:30,359 --> 00:01:32,181
Andhra Pradesh was split in two.

33
00:01:32,401 --> 00:01:33,762
Telangana became a new state.

34
00:01:34,182 --> 00:01:35,743
Hyderabad went to Telangana.

35
00:01:36,083 --> 00:01:37,264
What was left for Andhra?

36
00:01:37,544 --> 00:01:38,445
A long coastline.

37
00:01:38,705 --> 00:01:39,746
The Krishna and the Godavari.

38
00:01:40,446 --> 00:01:41,867
Lakhs of talented young people.

39
00:01:42,107 --> 00:01:43,188
But no capital.

40
00:01:43,508 --> 00:01:44,389
No IT hub.

41
00:01:44,509 --> 00:01:45,449
No Hyderabad.

42
00:01:45,730 --> 00:01:47,451
Now think about Chandrababu Naidu.

43
00:01:47,451 --> 00:01:52,674
From 1995 to 2004, he was CM of united Andhra
Pradesh.

44
00:01:52,854 --> 00:01:54,756
HITEC City came up in his time.

45
00:01:55,136 --> 00:01:56,777
The name "Cyberabad" was born.

46
00:01:57,177 --> 00:02:00,079
Microsoft and IT companies came to Hyderabad.

47
00:02:00,399 --> 00:02:03,401
He earned the brand "IT CM".

48
00:02:03,461 --> 00:02:07,084
And the city behind that brand — is now in
another state.

49
00:02:07,084 --> 00:02:09,805
In 2014, CBN became CM again.

50
00:02:10,106 --> 00:02:12,007
He chose Amaravati as the capital.

51
00:02:12,387 --> 00:02:15,569
The foundation stone was laid on October 22,
2015.

52
00:02:15,569 --> 00:02:15,570
The foundation stone was laid.

53
00:02:15,570 --> 00:02:21,300
Then in 2019, YSRCP won, and Jagan Mohan Reddy
brought in a "three capitals" plan —

54
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:25,620
Amaravati as the legislative capital, Kurnool
the judicial capital, and Vizag the executive

55
00:02:25,620 --> 00:02:26,000
capital.

56
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Did you notice something? For CBN it was
Amaravati; for Jagan, Vizag.

57
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:36,600
Their plans were different — but neither of
them ignored Vizag.

58
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:41,266
Next, in 2024, the TDP–Janasena–BJP alliance
came to power.

59
00:02:41,626 --> 00:02:42,907
CBN became CM again.

60
00:02:43,227 --> 00:02:48,795
While continuing with Amaravati as the
capital, he has now given Vizag a new role —

61
00:02:48,795 --> 00:02:50,472
Andhra's economic engine.

62
00:02:50,812 --> 00:02:52,994
You can see this directly on the ground in
Vizag.

63
00:02:53,334 --> 00:02:59,081
Naidu has called Vizag the centre of his
'Swarna Andhra' vision — the state's financial

64
00:02:59,081 --> 00:03:00,799
nucleus and knowledge hub.

65
00:03:01,039 --> 00:03:06,429
Put simply: Amaravati will run the
administration, and Vizag will earn money for

66
00:03:06,429 --> 00:03:07,103
the state.

67
00:03:07,443 --> 00:03:13,167
But the real question is — with so many cities
in Andhra, why Vizag?

68
00:03:14,268 --> 00:03:15,529
Chapter 2: Why

69
00:03:15,669 --> 00:03:16,469
Vizag?

70
00:03:16,890 --> 00:03:19,451
They call Vizag the "City of Destiny".

71
00:03:19,752 --> 00:03:23,314
That name didn't come by accident — there are
solid reasons behind it.

72
00:03:23,894 --> 00:03:25,635
First: the sea.

73
00:03:26,136 --> 00:03:31,439
Vizag has a natural deep harbour — a safe bay
surrounded by hills.

74
00:03:31,739 --> 00:03:36,583
For ships, cargo and heavy industry, that is
literally like gold.

75
00:03:36,743 --> 00:03:38,484
Second: the Navy.

76
00:03:38,484 --> 00:03:43,728
The Indian Navy's Eastern Naval Command is
headquartered in Vizag — making it a strategic

77
00:03:43,728 --> 00:03:45,849
city for India in the Bay of Bengal.

78
00:03:45,869 --> 00:03:49,651
Third: an industrial base that already exists.

79
00:03:49,991 --> 00:03:55,100
The Vizag Steel Plant, the refinery, the port,
pharma — industrial culture is nothing new to

80
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:55,655
this city.

81
00:03:55,675 --> 00:04:00,218
With around 25 lakh people, it is a ready-made
city.

82
00:04:00,298 --> 00:04:03,080
Fourth: resilience.

83
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:09,428
On October 12, 2014, Cyclone Hudhud hit Vizag
hard; the whole city was devastated, yet it

84
00:04:09,428 --> 00:04:11,846
stood back up within a few months.

85
00:04:12,166 --> 00:04:15,468
For big investors, this comeback story matters
a lot.

86
00:04:15,768 --> 00:04:18,830
But do you know the real game changer, bigger
than all of these?

87
00:04:19,291 --> 00:04:21,552
Wires under the sea.

88
00:04:21,972 --> 00:04:23,654
Yes — subsea cables.

89
00:04:23,814 --> 00:04:29,474
YouTube, WhatsApp, Gemini on our phones — all
that data travels around the world through

90
00:04:29,474 --> 00:04:31,018
cables on the sea floor.

91
00:04:31,359 --> 00:04:34,761
The point where those cables come ashore is
called a landing station.

92
00:04:35,221 --> 00:04:40,925
According to Google Cloud CEO Thomas Kurian,
the Vizag data centre will be connected by

93
00:04:40,925 --> 00:04:45,908
subsea cable to Singapore, Malaysia, Australia
— linking it to 12 countries.

94
00:04:46,208 --> 00:04:52,588
Here's another shocking number: nearly one in
five pieces of the world's digital data comes

95
00:04:52,588 --> 00:04:58,196
from India — but India's share of global
data-centre capacity is only 3 percent.

96
00:04:58,817 --> 00:05:02,419
Demand is enormous; supply isn't there.

97
00:05:02,639 --> 00:05:07,242
To fill that gap you need a coast, cables,
land and power.

98
00:05:07,683 --> 00:05:10,805
Andhra has the coastline; cables are coming to
Vizag.

99
00:05:11,125 --> 00:05:16,428
Long story short… the world's big tech
companies have started looking towards Vizag.

100
00:05:17,069 --> 00:05:18,610
Chapter 3: The

101
00:05:18,730 --> 00:05:22,853
Big Bets. Now let's look at the big bets
placed on Vizag, one by one.

102
00:05:23,233 --> 00:05:25,614
These numbers will make your head spin.

103
00:05:25,694 --> 00:05:29,917
Bet number 1 — the Google AI Hub.

104
00:05:30,418 --> 00:05:36,871
On October 14, 2025, in New Delhi, an MoU was
signed between the AP IT department and

105
00:05:36,871 --> 00:05:37,402
Google.

106
00:05:37,402 --> 00:05:46,380
An investment of 15 billion dollars over 5
years, from 2026 to 2030 — about 1.3 lakh

107
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:47,769
crore rupees.

108
00:05:48,129 --> 00:05:52,792
This is the biggest data centre Google is
building outside the United States.

109
00:05:52,832 --> 00:05:59,150
On April 28, 2026, CM Chandrababu Naidu and
Union IT Minister Ashwini Vaishnaw laid the

110
00:05:59,150 --> 00:06:01,038
foundation stone together.

111
00:06:01,378 --> 00:06:08,372
That day Vaishnaw said: "Visakhapatnam will be
born as AI-Patnam." With 1 gigawatt capacity,

112
00:06:08,372 --> 00:06:14,987
it is being built across three campuses —
Tarluvada, Adavivaram and Rambilli — on about

113
00:06:14,987 --> 00:06:15,747
600 acres.

114
00:06:16,148 --> 00:06:21,754
The project is being built with AdaniConneX, a
joint venture of the Adani Group and

115
00:06:21,754 --> 00:06:24,253
EdgeConneX; Airtel is also a partner.

116
00:06:24,313 --> 00:06:27,975
Bet number 2 — Data-centre city.

117
00:06:28,436 --> 00:06:34,230
It's not just Google — a Reliance, Brookfield
and Digital Realty joint venture is also

118
00:06:34,230 --> 00:06:38,542
putting 11 billion dollars into another AI
data centre in Vizag.

119
00:06:38,823 --> 00:06:44,926
The state government says agreements have been
signed for about 9 gigawatts of data-centre

120
00:06:44,926 --> 00:06:47,028
capacity around Vizag in total.

121
00:06:47,208 --> 00:06:48,909
Bet number 3 — Steel city.

122
00:06:49,309 --> 00:06:54,022
On March 23, 2026, at Rajayyapeta in
Nakkapalli mandal, Anakapalli district, CBN

123
00:06:54,022 --> 00:06:57,615
laid the foundation for the ArcelorMittal
Nippon Steel plant.

124
00:06:57,615 --> 00:07:04,836
With an investment of 1.36 lakh crore, on
5,465 acres, in two phases, it will have a

125
00:07:04,836 --> 00:07:08,102
total capacity of 17.8 million tonnes.

126
00:07:08,462 --> 00:07:13,920
CBN said then: "We are not building a steel
plant — we are building a steel city." Bet

127
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:15,507
number 4 — a new airport.

128
00:07:15,967 --> 00:07:22,266
PM Modi inaugurated the Alluri Sitarama Raju
International Airport at Bhogapuram in August

129
00:07:22,266 --> 00:07:27,515
2026, and from August 17 all flights moved
here from the old Vizag airport.

130
00:07:27,895 --> 00:07:32,278
The original deadline was December 2026, but
it was ready six months early.

131
00:07:32,638 --> 00:07:38,833
The old airport was just a civilian enclave
inside the Navy's INS Dega — now Vizag has its

132
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:40,623
own international airport.

133
00:07:41,164 --> 00:07:43,225
Bet number 5 — The master plan.

134
00:07:43,725 --> 00:07:46,487
The Visakhapatnam Economic Region — VER.

135
00:07:46,827 --> 00:07:53,822
From Srikakulam to Konaseema, with a target of
9.3 lakh crore in investments by 2032, and a

136
00:07:53,822 --> 00:07:56,974
"Bay City" project planned at its centre.

137
00:07:57,895 --> 00:08:04,918
Ports, airports, AI, fintech, tourism — the
plan is to turn North Andhra into one economic

138
00:08:04,918 --> 00:08:05,620
corridor.

139
00:08:05,640 --> 00:08:12,267
And at the 31st CII Partnership Summit held in
Vizag on November 12 and 13, representatives

140
00:08:12,267 --> 00:08:17,147
from 58 countries came and signed MoUs worth
lakhs of crores again.

141
00:08:17,608 --> 00:08:19,909
Hold on for a minute here.

142
00:08:20,369 --> 00:08:23,912
MoUs are only promises — not real investment.

143
00:08:24,212 --> 00:08:29,372
Not every rupee signed reaches the ground —
that's common to any government, in Andhra or

144
00:08:29,372 --> 00:08:30,416
anywhere in India.

145
00:08:31,117 --> 00:08:35,370
So the real question is — out of these lakhs
of crores, what does the ordinary Andhra

146
00:08:35,370 --> 00:08:35,920
person get?

147
00:08:35,940 --> 00:08:43,064
Chapter 4: What's

148
00:08:43,064 --> 00:08:43,864
In It For Andhra?

149
00:08:43,545 --> 00:08:47,347
There are lakhs of people like our Ravi in
North Andhra.

150
00:08:47,347 --> 00:08:52,336
Educated young people, construction workers,
IT engineers, nurses from Srikakulam,

151
00:08:52,336 --> 00:08:57,934
Vizianagaram, Vizag and Anakapalli — all going
to Hyderabad, Bangalore, Chennai or the Gulf.

152
00:08:58,495 --> 00:09:03,738
The government's pitch is simple: "Your
children no longer need to leave — the jobs

153
00:09:03,738 --> 00:09:09,233
will come here." Looking at the numbers, the
company says the ArcelorMittal steel plant

154
00:09:09,233 --> 00:09:14,665
will create about 1 lakh direct and indirect
jobs during construction and development.

155
00:09:15,065 --> 00:09:22,513
According to Google, the Vizag data centre
will generate 688 million dollars in local

156
00:09:22,513 --> 00:09:28,734
economic activity every year, and about 4,200
jobs during construction.

157
00:09:29,075 --> 00:09:35,638
With a 25,000-metric-tonne cargo terminal at
Bhogapuram airport, North Andhra's seafood,

158
00:09:35,638 --> 00:09:40,262
pharma and horticulture can be exported
directly to the world.

159
00:09:40,642 --> 00:09:43,884
Another emotional angle — the Vizag Steel
Plant.

160
00:09:44,205 --> 00:09:49,538
We all know the slogan "Visakha Steel is
Andhra's right"; on the new steel plant's

161
00:09:49,538 --> 00:09:55,067
foundation day, central ministers promised
financial support to RINL and to raise its

162
00:09:55,067 --> 00:09:55,652
capacity.

163
00:09:55,932 --> 00:10:01,239
Now the political angle: this bet is crucial
for Chandrababu Naidu because his whole

164
00:10:01,239 --> 00:10:03,577
political brand rests on development.

165
00:10:03,898 --> 00:10:10,556
HITEC City in Hyderabad gave him his first
legacy; if an AI city truly stands up in

166
00:10:10,556 --> 00:10:13,604
Vizag, that will be his second legacy.

167
00:10:13,984 --> 00:10:18,607
Otherwise, these lakhs of crores in MoUs will
remain only headlines.

168
00:10:18,907 --> 00:10:20,448
But here is the big twist.

169
00:10:20,889 --> 00:10:28,340
In the same statement, Google wrote another
line — once operations start in 2028, the

170
00:10:28,340 --> 00:10:33,337
permanent specialist jobs will only be in the
"hundreds".

171
00:10:33,337 --> 00:10:37,740
Hundreds of jobs for a 15-billion-dollar
investment?

172
00:10:37,860 --> 00:10:40,322
That's the critics' first question.

173
00:10:40,762 --> 00:10:46,366
As one activist put it: "We need mass
employment and labour-intensive industries —

174
00:10:46,366 --> 00:10:52,379
not high-capital industries." Because data
centres need a lot of land, a lot of power, a

175
00:10:52,379 --> 00:10:54,771
lot of water — but very few people.

176
00:10:55,111 --> 00:10:56,872
That's where the real fight begins.

177
00:10:57,553 --> 00:10:58,854
Chapter 5: The

178
00:10:58,954 --> 00:11:02,696
Backlash. Now let's look at the other side of
the coin.

179
00:11:02,696 --> 00:11:08,761
In September 2026, aerial photos of Tarluvada
village came out — hills cleared by

180
00:11:08,761 --> 00:11:13,403
excavators; once-green land now looks the
colour of red earth.

181
00:11:13,744 --> 00:11:18,827
Many people in Vizag fear three things: water,
electricity, jobs.

182
00:11:19,708 --> 00:11:25,983
Their complaint: data centres will draw water
and power, the environment will take a hit —

183
00:11:25,983 --> 00:11:28,633
but very few jobs will come in return.

184
00:11:29,214 --> 00:11:30,495
First concern — water.

185
00:11:30,855 --> 00:11:35,186
There's been a big objection to the project
near Adavivaram and Mudasarlova, because

186
00:11:35,186 --> 00:11:38,640
Mudasarlova is the reservoir that supplies
drinking water to Vizag.

187
00:11:39,160 --> 00:11:41,042
Human Rights Forum member V.S.

188
00:11:41,122 --> 00:11:47,369
Krishna asked a direct question: "Can anyone
imagine a data centre 120 metres from a

189
00:11:47,369 --> 00:11:54,285
drinking-water reservoir?" In May a video went
viral, in which a woman holding two jars — one

190
00:11:54,285 --> 00:12:01,052
with clean water, one with brown, muddy water
— alleged the data-centre construction caused

191
00:12:01,052 --> 00:12:01,275
it.

192
00:12:01,355 --> 00:12:02,996
Second concern — land.

193
00:12:03,496 --> 00:12:09,022
Professor Khairagi Reddy, honorary president
of Green Visakhapatnam, alleged that 160 acres

194
00:12:09,022 --> 00:12:14,548
belonging to the Simhachalam Devasthanam were
given to the Google–Adani data centre without

195
00:12:14,548 --> 00:12:17,766
an environmental impact assessment or public
hearing.

196
00:12:18,486 --> 00:12:22,569
These sites are also very close to the
Kambalakonda wildlife sanctuary.

197
00:12:22,689 --> 00:12:24,270
Third concern — clearances.

198
00:12:24,650 --> 00:12:30,503
In June 2026, the AP State Environment Impact
Assessment Authority granted Environmental

199
00:12:30,503 --> 00:12:33,696
Clearance to the Adavivaram–Mudasarlova
project.

200
00:12:33,796 --> 00:12:38,907
The HRF called it a "brazen injustice",
alleging that site works happened before the

201
00:12:38,907 --> 00:12:39,820
clearance came.

202
00:12:40,040 --> 00:12:44,243
On top of that, Vizag is a cyclone-prone coast
— we haven't forgotten Hudhud.

203
00:12:44,303 --> 00:12:46,845
Fourth concern — silencing voices.

204
00:12:47,345 --> 00:12:53,463
On July 27, 2026, police detained Left party
leaders who were going to meet people who had

205
00:12:53,463 --> 00:12:59,173
lost land in Tarluvada; the HRF alleged it was
an attempt to stop public discussion.

206
00:12:59,813 --> 00:13:04,416
Groups like Green Visakha held awareness
protests on Vizag's Beach Road.

207
00:13:05,057 --> 00:13:06,478
So what does the government say?

208
00:13:06,998 --> 00:13:13,572
IT Minister Nara Lokesh strongly defended the
project — his argument: "A 1 GW thermal power

209
00:13:13,572 --> 00:13:17,545
plant uses 7 times more water than a 1 GW data
centre."

210
00:13:17,885 --> 00:13:24,098
The clearances given to the two data-centre
parks name the Rural Water Supply department

211
00:13:24,098 --> 00:13:25,510
as the water source.

212
00:13:25,871 --> 00:13:31,391
The government's message: this is for the
future of Andhra's youth, and every big

213
00:13:31,391 --> 00:13:33,095
project faces opposition.

214
00:13:33,556 --> 00:13:39,302
But this isn't just Vizag's problem — the same
fight is happening over AI data centres around

215
00:13:39,302 --> 00:13:39,920
the world.

216
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:46,056
In Finland too, an authority ordered work to
stop at two Google data-centre sites until a

217
00:13:46,056 --> 00:13:48,866
mandatory environmental assessment is done.

218
00:13:49,186 --> 00:13:55,010
So the question here isn't "data centre — yes
or no" — it's "Where, how, and at whose cost?"

219
00:13:55,450 --> 00:13:57,772
Now another twist enters the story: politics.

220
00:13:58,332 --> 00:13:59,673
Chapter 6: The

221
00:13:59,793 --> 00:14:06,892
Credit War. For those who know Andhra
politics, this is no big surprise — when a big

222
00:14:06,892 --> 00:14:10,780
project comes, the first fight is over credit.

223
00:14:11,020 --> 00:14:13,902
First, let's look at YSRCP's argument.

224
00:14:14,242 --> 00:14:20,882
Jagan Mohan Reddy called Chandrababu a "credit
chor" and made some claims: that in November

225
00:14:20,882 --> 00:14:27,158
2020, during Covid, the YSRCP government
allotted land in Vizag to the Adani Group for

226
00:14:27,158 --> 00:14:33,288
a 300 MW data centre; the foundation stone was
laid on May 3, 2023; and the 3,900 km

227
00:14:33,288 --> 00:14:37,958
Singapore–Vizag subsea cable project also
started in their time.

228
00:14:38,198 --> 00:14:43,537
Jagan argued: "What's now being shown as the
Google data centre is just an expansion of the

229
00:14:43,537 --> 00:14:48,642
original Adani project; Adani is investing
87,000 crore, and Google will take over once

230
00:14:48,642 --> 00:14:49,346
it's built."

231
00:14:49,746 --> 00:14:55,508
YSRCP leader Gudivada Amarnath went a step
further, alleging that CBN is hiding the Adani

232
00:14:55,508 --> 00:14:57,191
deal behind Google's name.

233
00:14:57,671 --> 00:15:03,916
Now TDP's argument: the TDP says the Adani
data-centre MoU was signed in January 2019

234
00:15:03,916 --> 00:15:09,279
itself — that is, by the then TDP government,
before YSRCP came to power.

235
00:15:09,599 --> 00:15:14,357
Their counter: CBN also attended the
ground-breaking, and the project was delayed

236
00:15:14,357 --> 00:15:15,062
under YSRCP.

237
00:15:15,403 --> 00:15:21,734
And the TDP argues that the 15-billion-dollar
Google deal came in October 2025, under the

238
00:15:21,734 --> 00:15:23,228
coalition government.

239
00:15:23,828 --> 00:15:29,767
The twist in the story: YSRCP MP Maddila
Gurumoorthy filed a PIL in the AP High Court

240
00:15:29,767 --> 00:15:31,653
against this Google AI Hub.

241
00:15:31,954 --> 00:15:37,945
Nara Lokesh seized on it to attack YSRCP as
"anti-development"; Jagan countered again with

242
00:15:37,945 --> 00:15:41,340
the state budget, debts and corruption
allegations.

243
00:15:41,700 --> 00:15:47,687
So the scene is: one party says "this is our
project" while its own MP challenges the

244
00:15:47,687 --> 00:15:52,547
project in court; the other party says "this
is entirely our vision".

245
00:15:52,707 --> 00:15:58,817
The reality: from 2019 to 2026, both
governments have been involved with this

246
00:15:58,817 --> 00:15:59,452
project.

247
00:15:59,552 --> 00:16:04,446
But whoever gets the credit, it doesn't matter
much to the farmer in Tarluvada who lost his

248
00:16:04,446 --> 00:16:04,715
land.

249
00:16:05,556 --> 00:16:08,177
Nor to the family that drinks Mudasarlova's
water.

250
00:16:08,438 --> 00:16:10,699
Nor to our Ravi sitting in Hyderabad.

251
00:16:11,059 --> 00:16:15,242
What they need is just one thing — will this
project actually happen on the ground?

252
00:16:16,003 --> 00:16:22,467
And if it does, what will it give them, and
what will it take?

253
00:16:22,607 --> 00:16:24,908
Ending: Ravi's Choice.

254
00:16:25,529 --> 00:16:26,389
Sankranti is over.

255
00:16:26,469 --> 00:16:28,030
Ravi boards the bus to Hyderabad again.

256
00:16:28,391 --> 00:16:34,612
As the bus passes near Bhogapuram, he looks
out of the window — the new airport, new

257
00:16:34,612 --> 00:16:37,056
roads, hills cut in the distance.

258
00:16:37,217 --> 00:16:42,195
His mother's question comes back to him —
"Can't you find a job here?" For the first

259
00:16:42,195 --> 00:16:46,403
time, the answer in Ravi's mind wasn't "no";
it was "I don't know yet".

260
00:16:46,563 --> 00:16:47,603
That's the real story.

261
00:16:48,024 --> 00:16:54,148
Chandrababu Naidu has placed a big bet on
Vizag — not just CBN; every government that

262
00:16:54,148 --> 00:17:00,704
has ruled Andhra since 2014 has looked towards
Vizag, because after losing Hyderabad, it is

263
00:17:00,704 --> 00:17:03,514
the biggest ready-made city Andhra has.

264
00:17:03,554 --> 00:17:09,366
If this bet wins, Vizag becomes Andhra's
Hyderabad 2.0, and lakhs of people like Ravi

265
00:17:09,366 --> 00:17:10,939
can work close to home.

266
00:17:12,100 --> 00:17:17,318
If the bet fails — the hills will be gone, the
water will have dropped, and the MoUs will

267
00:17:17,318 --> 00:17:18,784
remain only in headlines.

268
00:17:18,804 --> 00:17:21,466
Now I leave you with three questions: 1.

269
00:17:21,466 --> 00:17:25,288
Can Vizag become Hyderabad 2.0 while
protecting its hills and water?

270
00:17:25,288 --> 00:17:26,569
2.

271
00:17:26,569 --> 00:17:31,913
Are data centres that create few jobs the
right bet for Andhra, or should it focus on

272
00:17:31,913 --> 00:17:33,674
labour-intensive industries?

273
00:17:33,674 --> 00:17:35,055
3.

274
00:17:35,055 --> 00:17:40,287
Is the credit for this project CBN's, or
Jagan's — or does it even matter to ordinary

275
00:17:40,287 --> 00:17:40,718
people?

276
00:17:41,119 --> 00:17:42,399
Tell us your answers in the comments.

277
00:17:42,880 --> 00:17:48,062
Share this video with your Vizag friends and
in North Andhra family WhatsApp groups — this

278
00:17:48,062 --> 00:17:50,825
conversation should happen in every Andhra
home.

279
00:17:51,265 --> 00:17:53,247
Thanks for watching. Jai Hind!
